        "prerequisite_note": "Developer-only separate logical package practice. Read installed records, cached metadata and supplied artifacts separately.",
        "concepts": [
          {
            "title": "The database is not the file",
            "text": "An installed record may still exist when an ordinary virtual file is absent or damaged. Recorded owner and payload inspection answer different questions."
          },
          {
            "title": "A logical repair has a declared boundary",
            "text": "Reinstall restores ordinary payload from the exact installed artifact. It preserves customized configuration in this script-free model. This is not a real dpkg transaction or rollback guarantee."
          },
          {
            "title": "Drafts and queries do not install anything",
            "text": "Filling proposed action fields changes only those fields. Explicitly perform the logical operation. Read-only queries and unused action drafts do not change current package outcomes."
          }
        ],
        "example_description": "In the separate gallery catalog, gallery-report is recorded as installed but its ordinary command text is missing. Preserve its customized configuration, peers, note and cached metadata while restoring the ordinary payload.",
        "example_actions": [
          {
            "action": {
              "kind": "Reinstall",
              "name": "gallery-report"
            },
            "explanation": "Fill the logical Reinstall target gallery-report. Inspect its local installed artifact and recorded file owner, then explicitly perform the logical action; Fill alone does not restore the file."
          }
        ],
        "try_change": {
          "description": "After the example passes, logically Remove gallery-report. The configuration remains but the installed/payload checks fail. Install the same package from the existing cached snapshot to repair.",
          "actions": [
